    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d178">

                <pb facs="0604" n="588" sameAs="frus:frus1951v01/pg588"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">600.0012/11–1951: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret   priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-11-19T19:00:00+01:00">November 19,
                            1951—7 p. m</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2994. Eyes only for Hickerson and Chase from Arneson. No further distribution.
                    Subject: Disarmament. To forestall any adverse comment from Baruch<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d178-f1"/> re disarmament debates in GA, Secy concurs in suggestion made by Jessup and Arneson that
                    Chase on strength of previous association reassure Baruch US stands firm on
                        UN plan as basis for internatl control to
                    ensure prohibition atomic weapons. [Arneson.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d178-f1" n="1" xml:id="d178-f1-content">
                <p>Bernard M. Baruch, New York financier; United States Representative on the United
                    Nations Atomic Energy Commission, 1946.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
